{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_015JwQaAewQM1wyYUUasNFSc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Anchor â€” what it is\n\n- **A personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty, built as a local-first markdown app.** Everything lives in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`) with plain markdown files as the source of truth â€” no database, no sync, no binary formats. Tasks, projects, inbox, and domain files (academic/commercial/family/writing) are all editable text.\n\n- **It ships `anchor_gui.py`** â€” a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server that renders a fully interactive dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, writing changes straight back to the markdown files. It runs persistently as the Windows NSSM service `anchor` (auto-start) on host PUTER/`gwl-server`.\n\n- **It ships `anchor.py`** â€” a CLI mirror of the same logic (done/cancel/save/add/capture/dashboard) that also generates the static `dashboard.html` and mirrors the R&D inspection commands.\n\n- **It supports a full task lifecycle** â€” Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, with archived tasks tracked in `CANCELLED.md` / `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`, plus daily logs and weekly reviews.\n\n- **It runs a daily self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`)** at 5:00 AM via Task Scheduler â€” parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint, walks a synthetic task through all states, and walks the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces fully stubbed. It writes `health_reports/YYYY-MM-DD.md` and shows a red dashboard banner on failure.\n\n- **Its largest layer is an \"R&D Control Surface\" for trio-driven development** (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). The newest version, **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built, 637 tests passed, merged to master `38fd70e`, 2026-06-13), turns each project's window into a single-screen cockpit: lane tiles (Research/Planning/Build/Deliverables/Grass) with one honest status light each, inline expanding panels that stack a summary over a real resizable terminal.\n\n- **The terminal substrate is real ConPTY** (`pty_manager.py` â†’ `terminal_session.py` â†’ xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket/SSE), with **per-session git-worktree isolation**, a durable session registry, cached/validated session + project summaries (generate-twice + grounding filter), stage handoffs, and ephemeral deliverable previews hard-guarded to never bind port 8777.\n\n- **It is deliberately stdlib-only with exactly one declared exception** â€” `pywinpty` (lazy import, `pty_manager.py` only, optional `pip install .[terminal]` extra). `distro.py`'s import scan enforces this and refuses any other native/third-party import in product code.\n\n- **It is branded as a Ghost World Labs tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\"** via a vendored brand mark, served as the dashboard favicon and masthead lockup.\n\nEverything above is drawn from the project's `CLAUDE.md` and locked North-Star/decision anchors; I haven't independently verified the test counts or merge commit against the live tree, but those are the figures the project documents record."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7264152-e287-4db5-b7a3-a9becc10ddd9","uuid":"0fdb8a23-05a9-48f8-80f8-e0b924a19c45","request_id":"req_011Cc1JBRug2Mj3H1snwid8D"}
